<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chait Singh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1810</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chait Singh was Raja of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varanasi">Benares</a> from 1770 to 1781, son of Balwant Singh. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warren-hastings">Warren Hastings</a>, Governor-General of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>, pressed him for extra payments and troops during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>'s wars, Chait Singh resisted; an attempt to arrest him in 1781 provoked a rising, and he fled to Gwalior territory. The affair became one of the main charges in Hastings's impeachment.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chait-singh.jpg" alt="Chait Singh" width="320" height="509" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maharaja_Chait_Singh_sahib_Bahadur_of_Banaras_State.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
